{
  "_comment": [
    "Excel function names by language. Hand-maintained and PARTIAL.",
    "",
    "CLDR does not model spreadsheet function names, and Microsoft's",
    "FunctionsTranslations workbook is not machine-fetchable, so there is no",
    "upstream to generate this from. Rather than guess at 500 functions across",
    "20 languages, this covers a high-confidence core and is built to grow.",
    "",
    "TO EXTEND: add entries under the language key. Keys are the canonical",
    "English name; values are that language's name. A function absent for a",
    "language resolves to its English name, which is also what the file format",
    "stores, so a missing entry is a display gap and never a wrong answer.",
    "",
    "NOTE ON USE: nothing in the transpiler reads this, by design. A workbook",
    "stores formula text in canonical English in the sheet XML regardless of the",
    "authoring language; Excel localizes only what it draws on screen. Codcel",
    "reads files rather than keystrokes, so no localized name ever reaches its",
    "parser. This table exists to render a formula back to a person in their own",
    "language, and as the prerequisite if a runtime formula parser ever lands."
  ],

